// Logos project — https://github.com/victor-smirnov/logos
//
// wql.peg — the wql! SURFACE grammar for peg_gen_logos, in SCHEMA-EMISSION mode
// (ADR 0012 peg-frontend). It builds the Phase-1 RQuery query-PLAN (the `RQuery`
// schema-enum family, `logos.std.wql.plan`) as first-class Writ schema views —
// `doc.make::<S>()` + typed field writes + `WRef<S>` edges — dogfooding ADR 0011.
//
// PARAMETERIZED surface (the trama! model): the macro is
//   resource <name> = deem!(<real Logos params>){ <query> };
// The PARENS carry a genuine Logos parameter list, re-emitted VERBATIM into the
// generated fn signature. SLICE params (`emps: &[Emp]`) are the query SOURCES —
// a `from`/`join` clause names one by its param name; the row type is the slice
// ELEMENT type from the param list (stamped onto the plan by the HANDLER after
// the parse — the grammar no longer captures `:[Ty]`). SCALAR params (i64 / f64
// / str / bool) are referenced BARE in the EL clause bodies (no `$` sigil; the
// old `with` clause is GONE — the param list is the single type source).
//
// The wql! surface has four shapes; each maps to one RQuery variant. The query
// body starts at `from` — the generated fn NAME comes from the enclosing
// `resource <name> =` binding (delivered as the handler's `name` arg and stamped
// onto the plan node's `fn_name` field after the parse):
//
//   RQSimple — from src var [where P]
//              select [first|distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
//   RQJoin   — from a x ( [anti] join b y on ON )+ [where P]
//              select [first|distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
//              (N-WAY CHAIN: each `[anti] join <src> <var> on <pred>` step is
//              one RQJoinStep in the RQJoinStepArr fan-out; a step's on-pred
//              may reference every var bound so far + scalar params. A step
//              source may ALSO be a FIELD PATH of a bound var —
//              `[anti] join <base>.<f>[.<g>…] <var> [on P]` — the TRAVERSAL
//              form (slice D): the new var ranges over the collection field,
//              `on` optional, is_edge/base_var/path on the step node)
//   RQAggr   — from a x ( [anti] join b y on ON )* [where P] group by K
//              aggregate name=fn(arg?),… [having H]
//              select [first|distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
//              (join steps OPTIONAL — aggregate over the joined stream)
//   RQFind   — from src var find P              (NO other clause — single-row
//              borrow: the generated fn returns Option<&Ty>, the first matching row)
//
// Pipeline semantics: where → group/aggregate → having → order → project(select)
// → distinct → limit. `having` exists ONLY on the aggregate shape (a predicate
// over the group key + aggregate output names); `order by` takes ONE key
// expression + an optional trailing `desc` (asc default); `limit` takes an
// INTEGER literal or a bare IDENT naming a SCALAR param from the deem!(…) list;
// `distinct` dedups the PROJECTED values; `first` (`select first S`) makes the
// query SINGLE-ROW — the generated fn returns Option<ElemTy> (the first
// projected value in scan order, or in ORDER BY order when `order by` is
// present). `first` excludes `distinct`/`limit` (diagnosed by the walker, not
// the grammar — both parse as independent OPT captures).
//
// ── EMBEDDED-EL CLAUSE BODIES (the ONE cross-grammar coupling) ──────────────
// Every EXPRESSION clause body (where / select / on / group-key / aggregate-arg)
// is EL — parsed by the generated EL parser (el.peg → `parse_expr`), producing an
// `SExpr` root handle wired into the plan node's `WRef<SExpr>` edge. Imported as
// `el`; each `<- el::expr` rule lowers to a cross-grammar embed call: scan the raw
// sub-range up to the next STRUCTURAL STOP and hand it to
// `logos.std.wql.el_parser::parse_expr(sub, doc)` into the SHARED arena.
//
// A WQL clause body does NOT end at a `}}`-style tag close (as Trama's does) — it
// ends at the next structural KEYWORD (rel/where/select/join/anti/group/by/
// aggregate/having/distinct/order/desc/limit/on), a top-level result-type `:`
// (ternary `?:` balanced), a top-level `,`/`)` (an aggregate arg list), or a
// top-level `;`/`}` (a rel-body terminator / rel-block close). The generator
// emits a KEYWORD-DELIMITED embed
// close-finder (`embed_find_close`) driven by this grammar's keyword tokens +
// `(`/`[` depth tracking — the schema-mode-gated generalization of the template
// close-finder (logos.peg has no embed, so its output stays byte-identical).
//
// ── REL BLOCKS (slice B — named derived relations, NON-recursive) ──────────
// Zero or more `rel NAME ( col: ty, … ) { body; body; … }` blocks may precede
// the entry query; the export is then the RQProgram ENVELOPE {rels[], entry}.
// Each rel body is a full `query` production terminated by `;` — the WALKER
// (not the grammar) restricts bodies to from/join/where/select, checks the
// select against the declared columns, enforces declaration-order rel scoping
// (self/forward/mutual reference → the recursion diagnostic; the fixpoint is
// slice C), and rejects f64 columns (set semantics require Eq).
//
// ── SELF-DESCRIBING (Option B) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
// source / var NAMES + the result type + aggregate column names live on the
// plan node as captured-IDENT `str` fields; the walker reads them directly (no
// side tables). Row TYPES are NOT grammar-captured any more — the handler
// stamps them from the param list. Optionality is an explicit `has_*` bool
// flag, derived from "did the OPT capture match" (a `bool` schema field written
// from a `$N` capture emits the presence test `capN != NULLP`).

%meta {
    name:      "wql"
    version:   "1.0"
    namespace: "logos::wql::surface"
    output:    "wql_surface_parser"
    package:   "logos.std.wql.wql_surface_parser"
    prefix:    "Wq"
}

// The wql! entry rule: a whole PROGRAM — zero or more `rel NAME(cols){bodies}`
// blocks followed by ONE entry query — → an RQProgram root edge handle (the
// program ENVELOPE; slice B static Datalog). A rel-less block still parses as
// a program (rels edge NULL), so the handler consumes one shape.
//
// `rel_list` is exported too. A `mapping` BODY is exactly a rel list with NO
// entry query, so it does not parse as a `program`. The mapping lowering parses
// the body ONCE through this entry and synthesizes a per-rel entry around the
// shared RQRelArr, rather than re-parsing the whole body once per rel.
%export { program rel_list }

// ── CROSS-GRAMMAR EL EMBEDDING ─────────────────────────────────────────────
%import "logos.std.wql.el_parser" as el

// ── SCHEMA-EMISSION binding ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The RQuery plan schemas live in `plan`; their `WRef<SExpr>` edge fields
// reference `SExpr` from the `ir` module — so BOTH are imported (one `use` per
// space-separated `use:` entry). `arena: external` → the export takes the
// handler's `&Writ`; `ref_wrap: "WRef"` is plan.logos's edge wrapper.
//
// Fan-out field type (generalizes el.peg's SExprArr `"argfan"`):
//   "fan set_agg  RQAGG_MAX"   spreads a $... array of RQAgg edges into RQAggArr
// The write is `while i<len && i<MAXFN() { node.METHOD(i, rcap.get(i)); i++ }` +
// `node.set_len(i)` — the same shape as `argfan` (= "fan set_arg SEXPRARR_MAX").
//
// A `bool` field written from a `$N` capture emits the OPT-PRESENCE test
// `capN != NULLP` (an OPT capture is NULLP when it did not match) — that is how
// `has_where` / `has_result_ty` / `is_anti` are populated.
// The SELECT-TAIL modifier fields (shared by simple/join/aggregate):
//   sel_first       — `select first …`        (OPT KW_FIRST capture presence;
//                     single-row mode — the fn returns Option<ElemTy>)
//   distinct        — `select distinct …`     (OPT KW_DISTINCT capture presence)
//   has_order/order_key/order_desc — `order by O [desc]` (order_clause? capture:
//                     presence + the key SExpr edge; KW_DESC? capture presence)
//   has_limit       — KW_LIMIT? capture presence (covers BOTH value forms)
//   limit_is_param/limit_param — `IDENT?` (a scalar-param name) presence + name
//   limit_n         — `INTEGER?` capture, token-text decoded to i64 (0 if absent)
%schema {
    use:      "logos.std.wql.plan"
    use:      "logos.std.wql.ir"
    arena:    external
    ref_wrap: "WRef"

    RQSimple      : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0000) cap(20) { src_name: "str" = 1, var_name: "str" = 3,
               has_gpath: "bool" = 18, gpath: "ref RQGStepArr" = 19,
               has_where: "bool" = 4, where_pred: "ref SExpr" = 5,
               sel_first: "bool" = 17, distinct: "bool" = 9, select: "ref SExpr" = 6,
               has_order: "bool" = 10, order_key: "ref SExpr" = 11, order_desc: "bool" = 12,
               has_limit: "bool" = 13, limit_n: "i64" = 14,
               limit_is_param: "bool" = 15, limit_param: "str" = 16,
               has_result_ty: "bool" = 7, result_ty: "str" = 8 }

    RQJoin        : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0001) cap(21) { a_name: "str" = 1, x_var: "str" = 3,
               has_gpath: "bool" = 19, gpath: "ref RQGStepArr" = 20,
               steps: "ref RQJoinStepArr" = 4,
               has_where: "bool" = 5, where_pred: "ref SExpr" = 6,
               sel_first: "bool" = 18, distinct: "bool" = 10, select: "ref SExpr" = 7,
               has_order: "bool" = 11, order_key: "ref SExpr" = 12, order_desc: "bool" = 13,
               has_limit: "bool" = 14, limit_n: "i64" = 15,
               limit_is_param: "bool" = 16, limit_param: "str" = 17,
               has_result_ty: "bool" = 8, result_ty: "str" = 9 }

    RQAggr        : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0002) cap(25) { a_name: "str" = 1, x_var: "str" = 3,
               has_gpath: "bool" = 23, gpath: "ref RQGStepArr" = 24,
               steps: "ref RQJoinStepArr" = 22,
               has_where: "bool" = 4, where_pred: "ref SExpr" = 5, key: "ref SExpr" = 6,
               aggs: "ref RQAggArr" = 7,
               has_having: "bool" = 19, having_pred: "ref SExpr" = 20,
               sel_first: "bool" = 21, distinct: "bool" = 11, select: "ref SExpr" = 8,
               has_order: "bool" = 12, order_key: "ref SExpr" = 13, order_desc: "bool" = 14,
               has_limit: "bool" = 15, limit_n: "i64" = 16,
               limit_is_param: "bool" = 17, limit_param: "str" = 18,
               has_result_ty: "bool" = 9, result_ty: "str" = 10 }

    RQFind        : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0003) cap(5) { src_name: "str" = 1, var_name: "str" = 3,
               pred: "ref SExpr" = 4 }

    RQAgg         : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0010) cap(4) { name: "str" = 0, fn_name: "str" = 1, arg: "ref SExpr" = 2, has_arg: "bool" = 3 }
    RQAggArr      : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0011) cap(9) { count: "i32" = 0, aggs: "fan set_agg RQAGG_MAX 8" = 1 }

    RQJoinStep    : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0012) cap(9) { is_anti: "bool" = 3, src_name: "str" = 0, var_name: "str" = 1, on: "ref SExpr" = 4,
                    is_edge: "bool" = 5, has_on: "bool" = 6, base_var: "str" = 7,
                    path: "ref RQPathSegArr" = 8 }
    RQJoinStepArr : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0013) cap(9) { count: "i32" = 0, steps: "fan set_step RQJSTEP_MAX 8" = 1 }

    // ── graph-path steps (ADR 0016 M2a) ───────────────────────────────────
    RQGStep       : code(0x0012_0000_0000_001C) cap(10) { is_key: "bool" = 0, is_elem: "bool" = 1, is_at: "bool" = 2, is_any: "bool" = 3,
                 is_desc: "bool" = 4, is_kind: "bool" = 5, key: "str" = 6, idx: "i64" = 7,
                 binder: "str" = 8, has_binder: "bool" = 9 }
    RQGStepArr    : code(0x0012_0000_0000_001D) cap(9) { count: "i32" = 0, steps: "fan set_gstep RQGSTEP_MAX 8" = 1 }

    // ── traversal-step field path (slice D — collection-field joins) ──────
    RQPathSeg     : code(0x0012_0000_0000_001A) cap(1) { name: "str" = 0 }
    RQPathSegArr  : code(0x0012_0000_0000_001B) cap(9) { count: "i32" = 0, segs: "fan set_seg RQPSEG_MAX 8" = 1 }

    // ── rel blocks + the program envelope (slice B static Datalog) ────────
    // cap covers the SOURCE-ORIGIN fields the COMPILER stamps after parsing
    // (src_file/src_line/segs — ADR 0024 S0). A TinyObjectMap's capacity is
    // fixed at construction, so the parser must size for writes it never makes.
    RQProgram     : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0019) cap(6) { rels: "ref RQRelArr" = 0, entry: "ref RQuery" = 1 }
    RQRel         : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0016) cap(3) { name: "str" = 0, cols: "ref RQRelColArr" = 1, bodies: "ref RQBodyArr" = 2 }
    RQRelCol      : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0014) cap(2) { name: "str" = 0, ty_name: "str" = 1 }
    RQRelColArr   : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0015) cap(9) { count: "i32" = 0, cols: "fan set_col RQRELCOL_MAX 8" = 1 }
    RQRelArr      : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0017) cap(9) { count: "i32" = 0, rels: "fan set_rel RQREL_MAX 8" = 1 }
    RQBodyArr     : code(0x0012_0000_0000_0018) cap(9) { count: "i32" = 0, bodies: "fan set_body RQBODY_MAX 8" = 1 }
}

// ── Tokens ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Structural keywords (declared as literal tokens; ordered before IDENT so
// `from`/`where`/… win). Every alpha-keyword literal ALSO drives the embed
// close-finder's structural-stop set (a top-level clause boundary).
%tokens {
    KW_REL       = "rel"
    KW_FROM      = "from"
    KW_WHERE     = "where"
    KW_SELECT    = "select"
    KW_ANTI      = "anti"
    KW_JOIN      = "join"
    KW_ON        = "on"
    KW_GROUP     = "group"
    KW_BY        = "by"
    KW_AGGREGATE = "aggregate"
    KW_HAVING    = "having"
    KW_DISTINCT  = "distinct"
    KW_FIRST     = "first"
    KW_FIND      = "find"
    KW_ORDER     = "order"
    KW_DESC      = "desc"
    KW_LIMIT     = "limit"

    // Punctuation.
    COLON    = ":"
    COMMA    = ","
    EQ       = "="
    LPAREN   = "("
    RPAREN   = ")"
    LBRACE   = "{"
    RBRACE   = "}"
    SEMI     = ";"
    DOT      = "."
    STAR2    = "**"
    STAR     = "*"
    LBRACK   = "["
    RBRACK   = "]"

    INTEGER = /[0-9]+/
    IDENT = /[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*/

    // Skip whitespace + line comments.
    %skip = /[ \t\r\n]+/
    %skip = /\/\/[^\n]*/
}

// ── Rules ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
%rules {
    // program := the whole wql! block — zero or more `rel` blocks + ONE entry
    // query → the RQProgram envelope. Alt 1 requires ≥ 1 rel block; alt 2 is
    // the rel-less form (rels edge stays NULL — `has_rels` on the schema).
    //   $1=rel_list $2=query        |        $1=query
    program <- rel_list query
               => { CODE: "RQProgram", rels: $1, entry: $2 }
             / query
               => { CODE: "RQProgram", entry: $1 }

    // ── rel blocks (slice B: named derived relations, NON-recursive) ──────
    // `rel NAME ( col: ty, … ) { body; body; … }` — each body is a full query
    // shape (the walker restricts bodies to from/join/where/select and checks
    // the select against the declared columns; declaration-order scoping +
    // the recursion diagnostic also live in the walker, which builds the rel
    // dependency edge list explicitly — slice C reuses it for the fixpoint).
    //   $1=KW_REL $2=IDENT(name) $3=LPAREN $4=rel_cols $5=RPAREN
    //   $6=LBRACE $7=rel_bodies $8=RBRACE
    rel_block <- KW_REL IDENT LPAREN rel_cols RPAREN
                 LBRACE rel_bodies RBRACE
                 => { CODE: "RQRel", name: $2, cols: $4, bodies: $7 }

    // The rel list (≥ 1) → RQRelArr fan-out (the join_steps pattern).
    rel_list <- rel_block rel_block* => { CODE: "RQRelArr", rels: $... }

    // One declared column: `name: ty` (ty ∈ i64/str/bool — walker-checked;
    // f64 is rejected there: set semantics require Eq).
    //   $1=IDENT(name) $2=COLON $3=IDENT(ty)
    rel_col  <- IDENT COLON IDENT
                => { CODE: "RQRelCol", name: $1, ty_name: $3 }

    // The column list (≥ 1) → RQRelColArr fan-out.
    rel_cols <- rel_col ( COMMA rel_col )* => { CODE: "RQRelColArr", cols: $... }

    // The body list (≥ 1, each `;`-terminated) → RQBodyArr fan-out. Every
    // body parses as a full `query` (an RQuery variant); `$...` collects the
    // query nodes (SEMI is a token capture — excluded).
    rel_bodies <- query SEMI ( query SEMI )*
                  => { CODE: "RQBodyArr", bodies: $... }

    // query := the whole wql! block → one RQuery variant.
    // Ordered choice (PEG first-match): the relational shapes are distinguished by
    // a structural keyword after the source; the leading optional `where` can
    // precede `group`, and `join`/`anti` can precede the select. Try join, then
    // aggregate, then the single-row `find`, then the simple scan/filter/project
    // fallback. Each alt re-parses the shared `from src var` prefix (cheap;
    // packrat-memoized).
    query <- join_query
           / aggr_query
           / find_query
           / simple_query

    // ── RQSimple ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //   from src var [where P]
    //   select [first] [distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
    //   $1=KW_FROM $2=IDENT(src) $3=IDENT(var)
    //   $4=where_opt? $5=KW_SELECT $6=KW_FIRST? $7=KW_DISTINCT? $8=sel_body
    //   $9=order_clause? $10=KW_DESC? $11=KW_LIMIT? $12=IDENT(limit-param)? $13=INTEGER?
    //   $14=result_opt?
    //   graph-path form ordered FIRST (≥1 gstep; the classic form can never
    //   shadow it — a bare `from src var` fails gsteps at the missing step).
    //   var_name is walker-stamped from the last step's binder.
    simple_query <- KW_FROM IDENT gsteps
                    where_clause?
                    KW_SELECT KW_FIRST? KW_DISTINCT? sel_body
                    order_clause? KW_DESC?
                    KW_LIMIT? IDENT? INTEGER?
                    result_clause?
                    => { CODE: "RQSimple", src_name: $2,
                         has_gpath: true, gpath: $3,
                         has_where: $4, where_pred: $4,
                         sel_first: $6, distinct: $7, select: $8,
                         has_order: $9, order_key: $9, order_desc: $10,
                         has_limit: $11, limit_is_param: $12, limit_param: $12,
                         limit_n: $13,
                         has_result_ty: $14, result_ty: $14 }
                  / KW_FROM IDENT IDENT
                    where_clause?
                    KW_SELECT KW_FIRST? KW_DISTINCT? sel_body
                    order_clause? KW_DESC?
                    KW_LIMIT? IDENT? INTEGER?
                    result_clause?
                    => { CODE: "RQSimple", src_name: $2,
                         var_name: $3, has_where: $4, where_pred: $4,
                         sel_first: $6, distinct: $7, select: $8,
                         has_order: $9, order_key: $9, order_desc: $10,
                         has_limit: $11, limit_is_param: $12, limit_param: $12,
                         limit_n: $13,
                         has_result_ty: $14, result_ty: $14 }

    // ── RQFind — single-row borrow: `from src var find P` ─────────────────
    // REPLACES where+select: the generated fn returns Option<&Ty> — a borrow of
    // the FIRST row matching P (early-exit scan), None when no row matches. NO
    // other clause may follow (the predicate body ends at EOI; a trailing
    // clause keyword fails the whole-query parse). Ordered BEFORE simple_query.
    //   $1=KW_FROM $2=IDENT(src) $3=IDENT(var) $4=KW_FIND $5=find_body
    find_query <- KW_FROM IDENT IDENT
                  KW_FIND find_body
                  => { CODE: "RQFind", src_name: $2,
                       var_name: $3, pred: $5 }

    // ── RQJoin — N-way join CHAIN ─────────────────────────────────────────
    //   from a x ( [anti] join b y on ON )+ [where P]
    //   select [first] [distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
    //   $1=KW_FROM $2=IDENT(a) $3=IDENT(x)
    //   $4=join_steps (RQJoinStepArr fan-out, ≥1 step)
    //   $5=where_opt? $6=KW_SELECT $7=KW_FIRST? $8=KW_DISTINCT? $9=sel_body
    //   $10=order_clause? $11=KW_DESC? $12=KW_LIMIT? $13=IDENT(limit-param)? $14=INTEGER?
    //   $15=result_opt?
    join_query <- KW_FROM IDENT gsteps
                  join_steps
                  where_clause?
                  KW_SELECT KW_FIRST? KW_DISTINCT? sel_body
                  order_clause? KW_DESC?
                  KW_LIMIT? IDENT? INTEGER?
                  result_clause?
                  => { CODE: "RQJoin", a_name: $2,
                       has_gpath: true, gpath: $3,
                       steps: $4, has_where: $5, where_pred: $5,
                       sel_first: $7, distinct: $8, select: $9,
                       has_order: $10, order_key: $10, order_desc: $11,
                       has_limit: $12, limit_is_param: $13, limit_param: $13,
                       limit_n: $14,
                       has_result_ty: $15, result_ty: $15 }
                / KW_FROM IDENT IDENT
                  join_steps
                  where_clause?
                  KW_SELECT KW_FIRST? KW_DISTINCT? sel_body
                  order_clause? KW_DESC?
                  KW_LIMIT? IDENT? INTEGER?
                  result_clause?
                  => { CODE: "RQJoin", a_name: $2, x_var: $3,
                       steps: $4, has_where: $5, where_pred: $5,
                       sel_first: $7, distinct: $8, select: $9,
                       has_order: $10, order_key: $10, order_desc: $11,
                       has_limit: $12, limit_is_param: $13, limit_param: $13,
                       limit_n: $14,
                       has_result_ty: $15, result_ty: $15 }

    // ── RQAggr ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //   from a x ( [anti] join b y on ON )* [where P] group by K
    //   aggregate a=fn(e),… [having H]
    //   select [first] [distinct] S [order by O [desc]] [limit N|p] [: RTy]
    //   (`first` PARSES here for a clear diagnostic, but the walker REJECTS it —
    //   group-by emission is multi-row by construction. `join_steps?` OPT: the
    //   steps edge is NULL when the aggregate ranges over a single source.)
    //   $1=KW_FROM $2=IDENT(a) $3=IDENT(x) $4=join_steps?
    //   $5=where_opt? $6=KW_GROUP $7=KW_BY $8=key_body
    //   $9=KW_AGGREGATE $10=agg_list $11=having_clause?
    //   $12=KW_SELECT $13=KW_FIRST? $14=KW_DISTINCT? $15=sel_body
    //   $16=order_clause? $17=KW_DESC? $18=KW_LIMIT? $19=IDENT(limit-param)? $20=INTEGER?
    //   $21=result_opt?
    aggr_query <- KW_FROM IDENT gsteps
                  join_steps?
                  where_clause?
                  KW_GROUP KW_BY key_body
                  KW_AGGREGATE agg_list
                  having_clause?
                  KW_SELECT KW_FIRST? KW_DISTINCT? sel_body
                  order_clause? KW_DESC?
                  KW_LIMIT? IDENT? INTEGER?
                  result_clause?
                  => { CODE: "RQAggr", a_name: $2,
                       has_gpath: true, gpath: $3,
                       steps: $4,
                       has_where: $5, where_pred: $5,
                       key: $8, aggs: $10,
                       has_having: $11, having_pred: $11,
                       sel_first: $13, distinct: $14, select: $15,
                       has_order: $16, order_key: $16, order_desc: $17,
                       has_limit: $18, limit_is_param: $19, limit_param: $19,
                       limit_n: $20,
                       has_result_ty: $21, result_ty: $21 }
                / KW_FROM IDENT IDENT
                  join_steps?
                  where_clause?
                  KW_GROUP KW_BY key_body
                  KW_AGGREGATE agg_list
                  having_clause?
                  KW_SELECT KW_FIRST? KW_DISTINCT? sel_body
                  order_clause? KW_DESC?
                  KW_LIMIT? IDENT? INTEGER?
                  result_clause?
                  => { CODE: "RQAggr", a_name: $2, x_var: $3,
                       steps: $4,
                       has_where: $5, where_pred: $5,
                       key: $8, aggs: $10,
                       has_having: $11, having_pred: $11,
                       sel_first: $13, distinct: $14, select: $15,
                       has_order: $16, order_key: $16, order_desc: $17,
                       has_limit: $18, limit_is_param: $19, limit_param: $19,
                       limit_n: $20,
                       has_result_ty: $21, result_ty: $21 }

    // ── Graph-path steps (ADR 0016 M2a) ───────────────────────────────────
    // `from g <step>* v`: steps over a GRAPH source (`g: &Writ`). A step may
    // be followed by a BINDER ident naming its edge row; the LAST step's
    // binder is the query row var (the walker stamps var_name from it and
    // REJECTS a bind-less last step). Steps never start with IDENT, so the
    // optional binder is unambiguous without lookahead. Lowered to a join
    // chain over the native edge relation in lower.logos.
    gstep <- DOT IDENT IDENT?
             => { CODE: "RQGStep", is_key: true, key: $2, binder: $3, has_binder: $3 }
           / LBRACK STAR RBRACK IDENT?
             => { CODE: "RQGStep", is_elem: true, binder: $4, has_binder: $4 }
           / LBRACK INTEGER RBRACK IDENT?
             => { CODE: "RQGStep", is_at: true, idx: $2, binder: $4, has_binder: $4 }
           / STAR2 IDENT?
             => { CODE: "RQGStep", is_desc: true, binder: $2, has_binder: $2 }
           / STAR IDENT?
             => { CODE: "RQGStep", is_any: true, binder: $2, has_binder: $2 }
           / LBRACE IDENT RBRACE IDENT?
             => { CODE: "RQGStep", is_kind: true, key: $2, binder: $4, has_binder: $4 }

    gsteps <- gstep gstep* => { CODE: "RQGStepArr", steps: $... }

    // ── Join steps (shared by join_query / aggr_query) ────────────────────
    // TWO step forms → ONE RQJoinStep node, discriminated by `is_edge`.
    // The PATH (traversal) form is ordered FIRST — it demands ≥ 1 `.field`
    // segment after the head IDENT, so the classic form can never shadow it
    // (PEG ordered choice; a classic `join b y on …` fails path_segs at the
    // missing DOT and falls through).
    //
    // TRAVERSAL (slice D): `[anti] join <base>.<f>[.<g>…] <var> [on P]` — the
    // step ranges over a COLLECTION FIELD of an already-bound row var; `on` is
    // OPTIONAL (containment IS the join; P is a residual filter). base_var +
    // the segment fan-out are grammar-captured; src_name/row_ty are WALKER-
    // stamped (full source expression text + reflected element type).
    //   $1=KW_ANTI? $2=KW_JOIN $3=IDENT(base) $4=path_segs $5=IDENT(var)
    //   $6=on_clause?
    //
    // CLASSIC: `[anti] join <src> <var> on <pred>` — `on` REQUIRED (unchanged).
    //   $1=KW_ANTI? $2=KW_JOIN $3=IDENT(src) $4=IDENT(var) $5=KW_ON $6=on_body
    // `row_ty` is handler-stamped (slice-param element type), like RQSimple.
    join_step  <- KW_ANTI? KW_JOIN IDENT path_segs IDENT
                  on_clause?
                  => { CODE: "RQJoinStep", is_anti: $1, base_var: $3, path: $4,
                       var_name: $5, on: $6, has_on: $6, is_edge: true }
                / KW_ANTI? KW_JOIN IDENT IDENT
                  KW_ON on_body
                  => { CODE: "RQJoinStep", is_anti: $1, src_name: $3,
                       var_name: $4, on: $6, has_on: true, is_edge: false }

    // `on P` — the traversal step's OPTIONAL residual (value = the SExpr, $2).
    on_clause <- KW_ON on_body

    // One `.field` path segment / the ≥1 segment list (RQPathSegArr fan-out).
    path_seg  <- DOT IDENT => { CODE: "RQPathSeg", name: $2 }
    path_segs <- path_seg path_seg* => { CODE: "RQPathSegArr", segs: $... }

    // The step list (≥ 1) → RQJoinStepArr fan-out (the agg_list pattern; every
    // capture is a join_step node, so `$...` collects exactly the steps).
    join_steps <- join_step join_step* => { CODE: "RQJoinStepArr", steps: $... }

    // ── Shared sub-rules ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
    // `where P` — the value is the predicate SExpr ($2, past the KW_WHERE token).
    where_clause <- KW_WHERE where_body

    // `having H` — aggregate shape only: a predicate over the group key +
    // aggregate output names. The value is the predicate SExpr ($2).
    having_clause <- KW_HAVING having_body

    // `order by O` — ONE key expression; the trailing `desc` is a separate OPT
    // token capture in the query rule (KW_DESC ends the embedded key body — a
    // structural stop). The value is the key SExpr ($3).
    order_clause <- KW_ORDER KW_BY order_body

    // `: <ResultTy>` — the value is the type-name IDENT ($2).
    result_clause <- COLON IDENT

    // The embedded EL clause bodies. Each `<- el::expr` is a cross-grammar embed:
    // scan the raw sub-range to the next structural stop, sub-parse into `doc`.
    where_body  <- el::expr
    sel_body    <- el::expr
    on_body     <- el::expr
    key_body    <- el::expr
    agg_body    <- el::expr
    having_body <- el::expr
    order_body  <- el::expr
    find_body   <- el::expr

    // aggregate list → RQAggArr fan-out.
    agg_list   <- agg_item ( COMMA agg_item )* => { CODE: "RQAggArr", aggs: $... }

    // One aggregate item: `name = fn(arg?)`. The empty-paren `count()` alt is tried
    // FIRST (PEG ordered choice) so it matches before the arg-bearing form.
    agg_item   <- IDENT EQ IDENT LPAREN RPAREN
                     => { CODE: "RQAgg", name: $1, fn_name: $3, has_arg: false }
                / IDENT EQ IDENT LPAREN agg_body RPAREN
                     => { CODE: "RQAgg", name: $1, fn_name: $3, arg: $5, has_arg: true }
}
